  "scope": "0.10.1-claudegpt.22: stage 2 slice 3 of the Rust migration. Additive PTY host protocol service sessions=1 (no protocol bump): the host works out each session's status from Claude Code hooks and the session registry as SessionManager does (UserPromptSubmit busy, Stop idle + done, Notification except idle_prompt waiting + waiting; registry polled once a second, stale entries ignored, changed status followed, WSL registry-only announcements, exit ends it) for sessions whose spawn meta carries claudeHome or wsl.share; event sessions.status { sessionId, instance, status, registry?, notify? } and list {} with the announcement held while detached; rust/reframe-sessions (no unsafe) with process alive/start from reframe-conpty; the Node host serves the same with the TypeScript registry readers; Electron takes status and notify intents from the host for those sessions and keeps its in-process path for the rest (older host or session, failed list); exit classification and whether to show a notification stay in Electron. Quota read: the 20 s deadline covers the wait too and kills on expiry; a fake Coordinator closeStdout case. Conformance replays hook/registry scenarios on both hosts against SessionManager as the oracle",
